    "title": "i2p: pass base32 address directly to stream connect",
    "user": {
      "login": "jpk68",
      "id": 256658809,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOD0xNeQ",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/256658809?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/jpk68",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/jpk68/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "As the SAM protocol accepts a `.b32.i2p` address as the `DESTINATION` parameter for the `STREAM CONNECT` command, the `NAMING LOOKUP` round trip can be skipped on every outbound connection.\n\nThis should ostensibly make failure handling more accurate in certain situations as well, since a peer that cannot be resolved now returns `CANT_REACH_PEER`/`TIMEOUT` rather than there being an empty `VALUE=` key in the lookup reply. A missing `VALUE=` is a proxy error, so the attempt isn't recorded in AddrMan.\n\nRouter implementation versions that support this (Java I2P 0.9.48, i2pd 2.38.0) are older than ones supporting `i2cp.leaseSetEncType=6,4` (see #35696), so there should be no compatibility issues here.\n\nSource:\nhttps://i2p.net/en/docs/api/samv3/#sam-virtual-streams-connect",
    "labels": [],
